cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its archived results, please cite the versioned Zenodo release."
type: software
title: "Broken Windows 311: Reproducible code and results for NYC and Chicago municipal service-request analyses"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible Python code, cleaned Jupyter notebooks, machine-readable result
  tables, figures, and provenance metadata for comparative analyses of municipal
  311 service requests in New York City and Chicago. The archive covers data
  preparation, fixed-effects and spatial models, responsiveness interactions,
  machine-learning prediction, SHAP explainability, heterogeneous effects, and
  cross-lag analyses. It excludes the manuscript and raw or analysis-ready data.
